      "content": "The opposition to vouchers is rooted in a fundamental belief in the public good and equitable funding for all children, not just a fear of change. Logically, critics point out that vouchers often benefit wealthier families who can afford associated fees at private institutions, exacerbating existing socioeconomic inequalities. Furthermore, they argue that withdrawing students from public schools reduces the necessary tax base and community investment in local education infrastructure.",
